meta {
  name: Upload Attachment
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/uploads/attachment
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file(C:\path\to\receipt.pdf)
}

script:post-response {
  const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (data && data.url) bru.setEnvVar("attachmentUrl", data.url);
}

docs {
  Upload one file to S3 and get its public URL. Form field name is **`file`**.

  Accepted types: PDF, JPG/JPEG, PNG. Max **10 MB**, otherwise 422
  `INVALID_UPLOAD_FILE`. Returns `{ "url": "https://s3-<region>.amazonaws.com/<bucket>/<key>" }`
  — store that string wherever an attachment URL is kept (e.g. pass it as
  `attachmentUrl` to **Receive Invoice Payment** / **Settle Settlement**).

  500 `UPLOAD_NOT_CONFIGURED` if the server's AWS_BUCKET / AWS_ACCESS_KEY /
  AWS_SECRET_KEY are unset. The bucket/prefix must be publicly readable (bucket
  policy) for the returned URL to preview in a browser.

  Edit the `@file(...)` path to a real file on your machine before sending. Run
  **Business Auth → Login** first so `{{businessAccessToken}}` is set.
}
